  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A cricket player catches a ball of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> moving with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> speed. If the catching process is completed in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> then the magnitude of force exerted by the ball on the hand of player will be(in SI unit):</p>",
